cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "diff-stream"
abstract: "Out-of-core difference-in-differences with staggered treatment timing: Callaway-Sant'Anna, Sun-Abraham, Borusyak-Jaravel-Spiess imputation, Gardner's two-stage estimator, Wooldridge's extended two-way fixed effects and stacked DiD, with the Goodman-Bacon decomposition and TWFE weights as diagnostics. Standard errors are clustered by unit and include the uncertainty in aggregation shares; fixed effects with many levels are absorbed with hdfe-stream. Results are tested against the authors' R and Stata packages."
authors:
  - family-names: Tucker
    given-names: Lee
    email: lee.c.tucker@census.gov
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/leetucker/diff-stream"
url: "https://github.com/leetucker/diff-stream"
keywords:
  - econometrics
  - difference-in-differences
  - staggered adoption
  - event study
  - treatment effects
  - two-way fixed effects
  - out-of-core
